<title>USA: Anicom acquires cable, connector maker.</title>
<headline>Anicom acquires cable, connector maker.</headline>
<dateline>ROSEMONT, Ill. 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anicom Inc said Monday it acquired Carolina Cable &amp; Connector Inc in a stock-and-cash deal valued at about $3.5 million.</p>
<p>Anicom said it will also assume $3.5 million in bank debt.</p>
<p>Carolina Cable &amp; Connector sells wire, cable, fiber optics and computer network products in the Carolinas and Tennessee, posting annual revenues of about $25 million in fiscal 1996, Anicom said.</p>
<p>Anicom is a distributor of multimedia wiring products.</p>
<p>Its shares were off 1/4 Monday at 10-1/4.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
